==Dungeon Crawl Summary==
A Dungeon Crawl is a form of instance available to players. It is in opposition to "Normal" instancing which supports respawning mobs for continuous farming. By contrast a Dungeon Crawl instance has a different ruleset based around non-respawning mobs.


{| style="background:transparent; width:100%;"
| style="width:50%; vertical-align:top;" |

===Dungeon Crawl (in-game data)===
Clear out the zone and you'll be rewarded for it.
* Nothing you kill will respawn naturally.
* To finish, slay every rare creature and enough of the zone's original population
* You'll earn motes and experience, and anything you killed may add its loot and coin to the reward pool.
* The easier the zone is for you, the smaller the payout
* Finish it and you get you instance charge back.
* Rare creatures show up more often, and you'll see them on your map

