===Random Bits of Details==
When starting a Dungeon Crawl, you simply select it on the right side of the instance selector; you can choose "Normal" or "Dungeon Crawl". Instance starts like normal with a zone-in, and warm-up phase for mobs.

[[File:dungeon_crawl_tracker_0.png|thumb|Dungeon Crawl Tracker]]
Players are given a new window to track process.

The tracker appears to track a bar with a number of general kills (percentage roughly), as well as the number of rare creatures in the zone.

The tracker is called the "Task Overlay window". You can set a hotkey for it in:
<code>Options > Controls > Key Bindings > All > Task Overlay window toggle</code>.

Lower Guk was giving me about 1% completion per 1.3 enemies killed (13 slain enemies at 10%)

It took 124 kills to get 100% general kills in Lower Guk, counting 25 Rare Kills

[[File:dungeon_crawl_map_named.png|thumb|Dungeon Crawl Map showing Rare Creature]]
Name enemies show up on the map just like with regular map "Mob Tracking", except they also show their name 

Rare creatures only show up on the map if they are within the range of your map "Mob Tracking"

Rare creature kills count as both "Rare Creature Killed" and General Population Kills

On Completion, a Reward Chest is given basically at your feet about 1-5 seconds after the last kill required. It appears to just be loot from the Zone you are hunting in, unsure on how much was regular loot and which are bonuses from Rare Kills.
[[File:dungeon_crawl_rewardchest.png|thumb|Dungeon Crawl Reward Chest]]

'''Teleporting rules apply:''' Using Gate, Ring, Circle, Portals, Succor:Location, Evac:Location, and their Rituals will drop you out of the instance (though you can re-enter the instance).<br>
''However'', [[Druid|Druids]] and [[Wizard|Wizards]] have an advantage because [[Lesser Succor]] and [[Lesser Evacuate]] do ''not'' take you out of the instance- They will take you back to the Evac point. If porting to the Evac point makes the crawl quicker, use it!

